# CVE-2022-25235 / CVE-2022-25236 (expat, "firefox" package): trivy's
# Ubuntu DB tracks the distro's own firefox, a snap-transitional stub
# versioned "1:1snap1-0ubuntu1" whose epoch compares newer than any
# Mozilla .deb ("<version>~buildN"), so the real, current Firefox is
# always reported vulnerable. aquasecurity/trivy discussion #6792.
# Same pair in desktop/xfce, apps/devtools, apps/hermes-agent.
CVE-2022-25235
